{"id":"word:hebrew:H4720","type":"word","title":"מִקְדָּשׁ","subtitle":"H4720 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a consecrated thing or place, especially, a palace , sanctuary (whether of Jehovah or of idols) or asylum","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to מִקְדָּשׁ (H4720) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 74 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"מִקְדָּשׁ (miqdâsh) means a consecrated thing or place, especially, a palace , sanctuary (whether of Jehovah or of idols) or asylum First listed occurrence: 1Chr 22 19."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"מִקְדָּשׁ","transliteration":"miqdâsh","pronunciation":"mik-dawsh'","strong":"H4720","lemmaId":"hebrew:H4720","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["הַ/מִּקְדָּשׁ֙","הַ/מִּקְדָּ֖שׁ","מִקְדָּשִׁ֔/י","מִקְדָּשִׁ/י֙","מִקְדָּשִׁ֛/י"],"morphs":[["HTd/Ncmsa",16],["HNcmsc/Sp1cs",13],["HNcmsc",6],["HNcmsc/Sp3ms",5],["HRd/Ncmsa",3],["HNcmsa",3],["HNcmsc/Sp2ms",3],["HR/Ncmsc/Sp1cs",3],["HR/Ncmsc/Sp3ms",2],["HR/Ncmsa",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"a consecrated thing or place, especially, a palace , sanctuary (whether of Jehovah or of idols) or asylum","usage":"chapel, hallowed part, holy place, sanctuary.","full":"H4720. miqdash or miqqedash מִקְדָּשׁ noun masculine Amos 7:9 sacred place, sanctuary ; — ׳מ Exod 25:8 +; מִקְּדָשׁ 15:17 (Ges § 20h Kö ii. 1, 471 ); construct מִקְדַּשׁ Lev 16:33 +; suffix מִקְדָּשִׁי 20:3 +, etc., מִקְדְּשׁוֺ Num 18:29 (Kö ii. 1, 97 ); plural מִקְדָּשִׁים Ezek 21:7 , construct מִקְדְּשֵׁי Jer 51:51 2 t.; suffix מִקְדָּשַׁי Lev 21:23 ; מְקַדְשֵׁיהֶם Ezek 7:24 (on anomalous pointing see Ew § 215 a Hi-Sm; but probably Pi`el Participle was in mind, Ges § 93oo Anm.; &lt; read מִקְדְּשֵׁיהֶם ); etc.; — 1 old Israel sanctuaries: of ׳י at Shechem Josh 24:26 (E); probably also Exod 15:17 (i.e. Shiloh); plural of sanct. to be destroyed by ׳י Lev 26:31 (H); יִשׂ ׳מִקְדְּשֵׁי in Northern Israel Amos 7:9 ; מִקְדַּשׁמֶֿלֶךְ vAmos 7:13 (Bethel). 2 of the nations: Moab Isa 16:12 plural of Tyre Ezek 28:18 (Co Toy [not Berthol Krae] read קָדְשְׁךָ thy sanctity ). 3 tabernacle and its precincts Exod 25:8 (P) +; הַקֹּדֶשׁ מִקְדַּשׁ Lev 16:33 , plural 21:23 . 4 temple and precincts 1Chr 22:19 ; Isa 63:18 ; Psa 74:7 +; מִקְדָּשָׁם בֵּית 2Chr 36:17 , הבית מקדשׁ Ezek 48:21 , מ ׳מְכוֺן Dan 8:11 ; plural of many sacred places in and about the temple. י בית ׳מִקְדְּשֵׁי Jer 51:51 ; אֵל מִקְדְּשֵׁי Psa 73:17 . Doubtful are: מִמִּקְדָּשֶׁיךָ Psalm 68:36 ( ᵐ5 ἐν τοῖς ὁσίοις αὐτοῦ ᵑ9 de sanctuario ; SS מִקְדָּשֶׁ֑ךָ ); מִקְדָּשִׁים Ezek 21:7 ( ᵐ5 Co Berthol Buhl מִקְדָּשָׁם ; Toy Krae מִקְדָּשֶׁיהָ ; || יְרוּשָׁלַםִ ); לַמִּקְדָּשׁ וּמִקְדָּשׁ 45:4 b (Co, after לְקָדְשָׁם מִפְקָד ᵐ5, [ לְבָֽתֵּי ]; Toy וּלְמִגְרָשִׁים [ לְבָֽתִּים ], compare Krae לְמִגְרָשׁ ). 5 ׳י will become ׳לְמ for his people Ezek 11:16 (Br MP 268 ), so apparently Isa 8:14 (but gloss Du Che Hpt Marti; Lag Semitic i. 16 מִקָּשׁ i.e. stumbling-block [he compare Syriac strike ]). 6 of ׳י s future sanct., ׳מ לעולם בתוכם Ezek 37:26 , 28 . &#8212; ( מִמֶּנּוּ ) אֶתקּמִקְדְּשׁוֺ ( מִכָּלחֶֿלְבּוֺ ) Num 18:29 even the hallowed part there of AV RV, but this not the meaning of ׳מ ; Ew § 255 c assumes מַ֗֗֗קְדֵּשׁ in this sense; &lt; read קָדְשׁוֺ (see קֹדֶשׁ 3d ), מִ being dittograph","rootNote":"or מִקְּדָשׁ ; (Exodus 15:17), from 6942 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 22 19","keyReferences":["1Chr 22 19","1Chr 28 10","2Chr 20 8","2Chr 26 18","2Chr 29 21","2Chr 30 8","2Chr 36 17","Amos 7 9"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":74,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 22 19","book":"1Chr","chapter":22,"verse":19,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מִקְדַּשׁ֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"1Chr 28 10","book":"1Chr","chapter":28,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לַ/מִּקְדָּ֖שׁ","source":"hebrew